This extension adds God of War: Ragnarok modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Auto-updates boot-info.json file. Supports Script-Loader.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]GoWR-Script-Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "winmm.dll" file and a "GOWR-Script-Loader.ini" file.[/*]
[*]Exec folder mods with an "exec" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Patch Folder mods with a "patch" folder install to the "exec" folder.[/*]
[*]Exec subfolder mods with an "ActivityFeed", "cinematics", "dc", "languages", "sound" or "wad" folder install to the "exec" folder.[/*]
[*]Texpack/Lodpack mods with a ".texpack" or ".lodpack" file install to the "exec\patch\pc_le" folder.[/*]
[*]Lua mods with an "int9" folder and a ".lua" file install to the "mod" folder.[/*]
[*]Save (Documents) mods install to the game's save folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Places .texpack and .lodpack mods into the correct folder automatically, based on how the files were packaged by the mod author.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff00]Includes Load Order support, and updates boot-options.json file with any .texpack and .lodpack mods installed.[/color][/b][/*]
[*]Automatically installs save games with mod type "Save Games (Documents)" to your GoW Ragnarok Documents folder.[/*]
[*]You can open the boot-options.json file and several other files and folders using the buttons in the Folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][b][color=#f6b26b]You can download the [url=https://github.com/Eiton/GoWR-Script-Loader]GoWR-Script-Loader[/url]﻿ using the button in the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/color][/b][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for God of War: Ragnarok mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Scriptloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "winmm.dll" file and a "GOWR-Script-Loader.ini" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Data:

Recognised when the archive contains a "exec" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Patchfolder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "patch" folder.

  Installs to: "exec"

========================================================================

Execsub:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ActivityFeed", "cinematics", "dc", "languages", "sound" or "wad" folder.

  Installs to: "exec"

========================================================================

Pack:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".texpack" or ".lodpack" file.

  Installs to: "exec\patch\pc_le"

========================================================================

Luamod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "int9" folder and a ".lua" file.

  Installs to: "mod"

========================================================================

Save:

Handled by the "testSave" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

